###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# About 240 GPU-h of unbiased and enhanced-sampling MD and about 43 GPU-h of MLIP training on an NVIDIA L40S, and about 72,000 CPU-h of Qbox DFT on Intel Xeon E5-2680 CPUs, over the six rounds (Sec. 3.1).

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Energy MAEs are stated only approximately ('around 0.001 eV/atom' in rounds 3-6), so they are not encoded; rounds 4 and 5 are figure-only (Fig. 3).
# - The 6 ns/day throughput is approximate and the system size is the default 216-atom supercell (Sec. 2.1); the paper does not tie the throughput to a system explicitly.
# - Force MAEs on the trivacancy and 10-vacancy 512-atom MD snapshots (Fig. 5, below about 0.10 eV/A) are figure-only; free-energy barriers (Table 1) are properties.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/dutta2026.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

